# 🌈 Improvements

## View the target state of dynamic search rules


> [!NOTE]  
> Using this feature requires the Enterprise Edition. Enterprise Edition features are also available on [Meilisearch Cloud](https://www.meilisearch.com/pricing).

Allows seeing the state of dynamic search rules (DSR) as if all pending DSR update tasks had been processed.

A "pending" task is a task that is either enqueued or currently processing.

### Route to see the target state of a selected rule

The new `GET /dynamic-search-rules/{:ruleUid}/target` route returns the "target" state of the DSR, that is, an object with the following fields:

- `current`, dynamic search rule object or `null`: the current values of the dynamic search rules, or `null` if the dynamic search rule doesn't exist yet
- `target`, dynamic search rule object or `null`: the field of the dynamic search rules that will be modified by currently pending tasks, or `null` if the dynamic search rule will be deleted after all pending tasks have been processed
- `needsProcessing`, boolean, `true` if at least one pending task pertaining to this dynamic search rule exists
- `taskUids`, array of task uids, list of the pending tasks pertaining to the dynamic search rule

### New body parameter to see the target state of all rules

The existing `POST /dynamic-search-rules` route used to list the dynamic search rules has a new `showTarget` parameter, an optional boolean. When present and `true`, `showTarget` modifies the response in the following way:

1. new global fields in the response:
    - `needsProcessing`: boolean, `true` if at least one DSR update task exists
    - `taskUids`, array of task uids, list of the pending DSR update tasks
    - `totalRuleCount`, number, current total number of rules regardless of the filter. This field is different from `total` in that `total` indicates the total number of rules matching the optional filter passed in the body parameters of `POST /dynamic-search-rules`
    - `targetTotalRuleCount`, number, total number of rules that will exist after processing all pending DSR update tasks
2. each rule returned in results has an additional `needsProcessing` boolean set to `true` if at least one pending DSR update task applies to this rule. 

### Examples

#### Creating a new rule and checking its target state

<details>
<summary>Creating a new rule</summary>

```jsonc
// PATCH /dynamic-search-rules/scale-rule
{
          "conditions": {
            "query": {
              "words": "HERO SUPER"
            }
          },
          "actions": {
            "scale": [
              {
                "ids": ["372631"],
                "weight": 2.0
              }
            ]
          }
}
```


</details>

<details>
<summary>Checking its target state before the task is processed</summary>

```jsonc
// GET /dynamic-search-rules/scale-rule/target

// response
{
        "current": null, // rule did not previously exist
        "needsProcessing": true, // rule needs processing
        "target": { // target state matches the update
          "actions": {
            "scale": [
              {
                "ids": ["372631"],
                "weight": 2.0
              }
            ]
          },
          "active": true,
          "conditions": {
            "query": {
              "words": "HERO SUPER"
            }
          }
        },
        "taskUids": [6] // id of the task that will create the rule
}
```

</details>

<details>
<summary>Listing the rules before the new rule has been created</summary>

```jsonc
// POST /dynamic-search-rules

// request body
{
  "showTarget": true
}

// response
